**********Source Check**********

The claim '1.  `Someone` theorized it would be a shell made up of mirrors or solar panels that completely surrounds a star — harnessing all the energy it produces.' is NOT supported by the citation.
<reject> The information is not explicitly mentioned in the content. While Freeman Dyson theorized the concept of structures to harvest stellar energy, the content does not explicitly state that these structures would be "made up of mirrors or solar panels." It mentions they would be "designed to intercept and collect its energy," which implies such materials but does not name them. Furthermore, while the concept "encompasses a star" and "captures a large percentage of its power output," it does not state "harnessing all the energy it produces." Lastly, while Dyson initially referred to it as a "shell," he later clarified he did not mean a "solid shell" but rather a "loose collection or swarm of objects," which contradicts the typical understanding of "a shell." </reject>

