The claim '2.  Dyson took the idea from `something`, and he was always open about that.' is supported by the citation.
<accept> The content explicitly states that Freeman Dyson was "inspired by" Olaf Stapledon's 1937 science fiction novel *Star Maker* and even quotes Dyson himself saying, "In fact, I took the idea from Olaf Stapledon, one of their own colleagues." It also notes that Dyson suggested "Stapledon sphere" would be a more apt name, which implies his openness about the origin of the concept. </accept>

